{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/BeatUnitTied\/beatUnitDot","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome\/beatunittied\/beatunitdot"]}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","title":"beatUnitDot","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"externalID":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLMetronomeV12BeatUnitTiedV04beatE3DotSivp","symbolKind":"property","roleHeading":"Instance Property","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"beatUnitDot"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int"}]},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/BeatUnitTied"]]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The number of augmentation dots to apply to the beat-unit note in a metronome mark."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"beatUnitDot"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Maps to a nested MusicXML "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<beat-unit-dot>"},{"type":"text","text":" element."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLMetronome/BeatUnitTied/beatUnitDot":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/BeatUnitTied\/beatUnitDot","role":"symbol","title":"beatUnitDot","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome\/beatunittied\/beatunitdot","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The number of augmentation dots to apply to the beat-unit note in a metronome mark."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"beatUnitDot"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLMetronome/BeatUnitTied":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/BeatUnitTied","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"BeatUnitTied"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome\/beatunittied","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"BeatUnitTied"}],"title":"MXLMetronome.BeatUnitTied","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The beat-unit-tied type indicates a beat-unit within a metronome mark that is tied to the preceding beat-unit."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"This allows two or more tied notes to be associated with a per-minute value in a metronome mark, whereas the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"metronome-tied element is restricted to metric relationship marks."}],"type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLMetronome":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The metronome type represents metronome marks and other metric relationships. The beat-unit group and per-"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"minute element specify regular metronome marks. The metronome-note and metronome-relation elements allow for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the specification of metric modulations and other metric relationships, such as swing tempo marks where two"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"eighths are equated to a quarter note \/ eighth note triplet. Tied notes can be represented in both types of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"metronome marks by using the beat-unit-tied and metronome-tied elements. The parentheses attribute indicates"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whether or not to put the metronome mark in parentheses; its value is no if not specified. The print-object"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"attribute is set to no in cases where the metronome element represents a relationship or range that is not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"displayed in the music notation."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLMetronome"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLMetronome","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLMetronome"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome","role":"symbol"}}}